      "blocks": {
        "description_1": {
          "type": "description",
          "settings": {
            "description_text": "<p>A job search is a small project with a lot of moving parts. Twenty roles, a dozen people, three interview loops and a deadline nobody wrote down.</p><p>Most of us run it from memory, a spreadsheet and an inbox. That works for the first week. Then a recruiter asks you to follow up on Tuesday and Tuesday passes.</p><p>Offer Board is the system we wished we had:</p><ul><li>every role on one board, with where it stands</li><li>every person with the next date to write to them</li><li>your best stories ready before each interview</li><li>offers compared on more than the salary</li></ul><p>It is plain on purpose. Six pages you will open every day and a review that takes twenty minutes on a Friday.</p><p>New to Notion? The walkthrough video covers everything you need.</p>",
            "description_text_size": 16,
            "description_mobile_size": 15,
            "description_left_padding_desktop": 330,
            "description_right_padding_desktop": 330,
            "description_left_padding_mobile": 4,
